1. IBM FastFit (code included in this repository)

   The directory soctriage/models/fastfit/ contains a modified copy of FastFit,
   developed by IBM (https://github.com/IBM/fastfit), which is licensed under
   the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   The copy has been modified by Torq Technologies Ltd. The modifications
   include: LoRA-friendly encoder handling, Apple-Silicon (MPS) fixes, a
   classification-head loss path with optional focal-Tversky loss, a
   soft-recall hinge, soft false-positive penalty and reward terms,
   and a malicious/non-malicious balanced batch sampler. Each copied file
   carries a notice attributing it to IBM FastFit and stating that it has been
   modified. No notices from IBM's original source files have been removed.
   IBM's original files contain no copyright notice other than the standard
   Apache placeholder line.

   The Apache License, Version 2.0 is reproduced in the LICENSE file.


2. Microsoft GUIDE dataset (data derived from it is included in this repository)

   Some files in this repository are derived from the GUIDE dataset published
   by Microsoft ("Microsoft Security Incident Prediction",
   https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/Microsoft/microsoft-security-incident-prediction).
   GUIDE itself is not included. A script is provided to download it. The files
   derived from GUIDE contain labels, incident and organization identifiers and
   per-prompt model outputs and predictions. These are the files in the
   data/guide/ directory, and any other files in this repository that contain
   labels, identifiers or predictions derived from GUIDE. The per-prompt model
   outputs in data/guide/ were generated by third-party AI models and are
   AI-generated content.

